            "kind": "TRIVIAL_REBASE",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/lib/log_services.hpp",
                    "line": 910,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "Spreading this check across a bunch of different branches is a mess to read.  I suspect we can just enforce this at configure time?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/lib/log_services.hpp",
                    "line": 910,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Oliver Brewka",
                        "email": "oliver.brewka@9elements.com",
                        "username": "mox669"
                    },
                    "message": "I don't think it is possible to do this check during configuration of the build. `systemName` is set at runtime with the incoming request. \n\nAm I overlooking sth?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/lib/log_services.hpp",
                    "line": 943,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Gunnar Mills",
                        "email": "gunnar@gmills.xyz",
                        "username": "gtmills"
                    },
                    "message": "So you just don't add the link ? \nSo LogServices is just empty when MULTI_COMPUTER_SYSTEM ?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/lib/log_services.hpp",
                    "line": 943,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Oliver Brewka",
                        "email": "oliver.brewka@9elements.com",
                        "username": "mox669"
                    },
                    "message": "> So you just don't add the link ?\n\nCorrect. \n\n> So LogServices is just empty when MULTI_COMPUTER_SYSTEM ?\n\nIt contains the PostCodes LogService, for which the follow-up patch adds support for multi-host."
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/lib/log_services.hpp",
                    "line": 952,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "See above, this one specifically, if these two options aren't allowed together, can we just make that enforced in meson?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/lib/log_services.hpp",
                    "line": 952,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Oliver Brewka",
                        "email": "oliver.brewka@9elements.com",
                        "username": "mox669"
                    },
                    "message": "For the log options I did solve this in meson. Done"
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/lib/log_services.hpp",
                    "line": 974,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "systemName{std::move(systemName)}\n\nDoesn't really matter in practice, but static analyzers complain."
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/lib/log_services.hpp",
                    "line": 974,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Oliver Brewka",
                        "email": "oliver.brewka@9elements.com",
                        "username": "mox669"
                    },
                    "message": "So do I need to change this? This is how we do it in multiple places apart from this patch\n\nAlso clang-tidy does not complain on my local machine, so I am a bit confused."
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/lib/log_services.hpp",
                    "line": 992,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "This is now a security vulnerability as you've written it.  \"systemName\" comes from the user, so might contain bad characters (including query strings and other stuff).  BMCWEB_REDFISH_SYSTEM_URI_NAME comes from compile time, so std::format is appropriate, although really anything new should use boost::urls::format"
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/lib/log_services.hpp",
                    "line": 992,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Oliver Brewka",
                        "email": "oliver.brewka@9elements.com",
                        "username": "mox669"
                    },
                    "message": "The follow-up patch already fixes that."
                }
            ],
